      "writtenOn": "2022-07-27T00:18:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e DT_CHOSEN(cros_ec_espi)\n\nI don\u0027t think a chosen node is correct here, because this code is tightly coupled to the SoC. If there were some kind of external eSPI controller that a board chose this code would not work correctly if it tried to use that device.\n\n\u003e rather than saving this as a static...\n\nI assume this can be trivially optimized to inline the resultant pointer (so there\u0027s no difference in generated code) and I think this way is nicer to read since it does things like show the reader what the type is.\n\n\u003e `device_is_ready()`\n\nDone.",
      "parentUuid": "02102faa_9844d02a",
